              <li>• The southern Berkshires are reachable via I-90 E in under 40 minutes</li>
              <li>• For the Catskills, take NY-23 or the NY Thruway (I-87) S</li>
              <li>• For southern Vermont, take US-7 N or VT-9 E</li>
              <li>• Download offline maps in case of poor cell service on back roads</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-2xl">🎒</span> What to Bring
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700">
              <li>• Water: 2+ liters per person</li>
              <li>• Snacks: Trail mix, energy bars, fruit</li>
              <li>• Layers: weather shifts fast at elevation</li>
              <li>• First aid kit & headlamp</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-2xl">📅</span> Best Times to Visit
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700">
              <li>• <strong>Summer (Jun-Aug):</strong> Best weather, most crowded</li>
              <li>• <strong>Fall (Sep-Oct):</strong> Peak Berkshires and Catskills foliage</li>
              <li>• <strong>Spring (Apr-May):</strong> Mud season on wooded trails</li>
              <li>• <strong>Winter (Dec-Mar):</strong> Lower Berkshire trails stay walkable with traction; Catskill and Vermont summits need full winter gear</li>
